<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5952" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">căco</span></b> , āvi, ātum,
			āre, v. n. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a.</i>,—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακάω</span>, <i>to go to
			stool</i>, <i>to be at stool.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>, Pompon. ap. <i><span class="en">Non.
				p. 84, 2</span></i>: toto decies in 
			 anno, <i><span class="en">Cat. 23, 20</span></i>; *<i><span class="en">Hor. S. 1,
				8, 38</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 12, 61,
			10</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, Pompon. ap. <i><span class="en">Non.
				p. 84, 1</span></i> (Com. Rel. p. 209 Rib.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">canes odorem mixtum cum merdis cacant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Phaedr. 4, 17, 25</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Mart. 3, 89</span></i>.—Also, <i>to defile with excrement</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cacata charta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					36, 1</span></i>
			 and 20.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
